# Line endings.
#
# The problem this solves is specific and bites on the first run: Git for
# Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. backend/entrypoint.sh and sandbox-runner/entrypoint.sh are COPYed
# into their images and used as ENTRYPOINT, so a CRLF shebang makes the kernel
# look for an interpreter literally named "/usr/bin/env bash\r". Docker then
# reports
#
#     exec /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# on a file that plainly exists, which sends people hunting for a missing
# binary that was never missing.
#
# Everything that runs inside a container, or that a container parses, is
# pinned to LF regardless of the host.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

*.py            text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.jsx           text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf

# Batch files are the exception: cmd.exe wants CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touched.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.svg           text eol=lf
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.gz            binary
*.zip           binary
